Refurbished Linux 0.3.0-r2 — UEFI boot fix (same system, corrected bootloader menu)

file:   refurbished-linux-0.3.0-r2-amd64.iso
size:   810549248 bytes (773 MiB)
sha256: 676c08c9532e75881a4119b0e5868c2b2fa0a15772030b7f5b575cff5eb06d27
firmware: BIOS (isolinux menu.c32) + UEFI (grub efi.img), isohybrid MBR+GPT
base:   Debian 13 trixie, kernel 6.12.117-amd64 (identical to 0.3.0)

Fixes the 0.3.0 failure "file /live/vmlinuz not found / you need to load
the kernel first" on UEFI machines: the GRUB menu now searches the live
medium instead of assuming $root, and no longer uses shell ${var:-default}
syntax that GRUB cannot parse. See docs/release-0.3.md.

Verified under OVMF (UEFI), 2 cores / 2 GB / TCG:
  - ISO as DVD (El Torito): 0 GRUB errors, desktop up
  - ISO as USB stick (dd-style): 0 GRUB errors, boot completes
  - docs/screenshots/0.3.0-r2-uefi-desktop.png
